{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1474143-resuscitate-an-ally","id":1474143,"title":"Resuscitate an ally","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-07T16:33:22-08:00","id":1474143,"title":"Resuscitate an ally","content":"If an ally is incapacitated by agg damage and fail to stay alive by rolling rage, he dies. But that's the same for a human with really bad wound and if a doctor managed to resusitate him soon enough (less than 5 minutes) he can be saved.<br /> There is no rule about that in the books i have, so i'm trying to houserule a way to save an ally or another player.<br /> <br /> First it has to be done in the same scene the poor victim has been incapacitated and the injury must not be too severe for resuscitation to be possible. The roll is Intelligence + Medicine and the difficulty is defined by the st depending on the severity of the injury.<br /> Where i can't state is how many success must be obtained to save the victim and how the stamina of the victim can be used to help the healer (more round to get the success or reduced difficulty on the roll)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 02-07-2022, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T01:47:49-08:00","id":1474174,"title":"","content":"You could require 7 minus the stamina of the patient as successes. When Stamina 2 is average for the general population, then it would require 5 successes, which is really difficult to obtain, but with certain tools, like an ambulance, it might be feasible.<br /> <br /> Generally, I'd agree that there should be a possibility to keep a incapacitated person alike, even when agg damage was the cause. In any case, there should be a Battle Scar remaining, if the healing wasn't magically.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T12:20:37-08:00","id":1474220,"title":"","content":"A batte scar is inevitable at this stage, but 7 seems a little too low, if the victim is a metis he will be in crinos form. With his bonus he could have 7 or 8 dots in stamina and the roll would be useless.<br /> It has to be an extended roll so maybe 10 minus 1 by stamina dots of the victim, and if the victim is really big the healer has to use proper instrument or supernatural abilities to affect the body","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-08T13:50:50-08:00","id":1474228,"title":"","content":"An extended roll like that would make sense. But I think it is harder to get drama out of it.<br /> <br /> I mean, if the PC A's life is saved by PC B's roll, it is one thing. If Player B has to roll three times to save PC A, okay - but depending on the dice pool and difficulty it can easily shift the situation from excitement and anticipation regarding the roll to annoyance.or a feeling of being set up to fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-09T01:34:49-08:00","id":1474268,"title":"","content":"Since the difficulty depend of the wound and that there is a limited time to resusitate the victim, a fail can be dramatic. A simple fail give nothing so the healer lose time to save the victim. This could be represented by a difficulty increased by one.<br /> If the injury is really bad then it will be harder for the healer to save him. A hole in the stomach, a broken neck, silver bullets in lungs etc will need surgery and on a battlefield that's really difficult to focus. The difficulty would be 8 or 9, maybe 10 in some case, so a botch is easily obtained on the roll, and a botch means not only that the healer fail to heal the victim but make a mistake and worsen the victim's situation (difficulty +2/3 according to the type of injury, another battle scar and if the difficulty get higher than 10, then it's too late to save him)<br /> <br /> Several healer can also work together and accumulate their succes to heal faster and better the victim or use a gift like mother's touch during the process to reduce the roll difficulty","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}